{"id":"property-value-25m-50m","version":2,"category":"property-value","when":"US$25,000,000–50,000,000 estimated property-value label, used only as a subjective design-ambition reference. Property value is not a construction budget. Location, land value, market conditions, condition and other factors affect prices; this band establishes no market-price or cost claim.","title":"Design-ambition reference: Exceptional estate: integrated architecture","combinations":"Terra may combine, reinterpret or omit these subjective ideas with relevant regional, style, climate, entrance, roof, facade, material and room-planning knowledge. Amenities are optional inspirations, never mandatory. Do not constrain creative freedom through a fixed template, geometry, area, storey, room or amenity count.","placement":"Let the household brief, site, climate, privacy and architectural concept determine spatial relationships. Connect arrival, shared living and sheltered outdoor space where appropriate; separate guest, private and service movement when useful. No fixed floor areas, storey counts or room counts follow from the value label.","principles":"Explore an estate-wide composition with a strong main residence, private suites, connected living and sheltered entertaining. Compose a bespoke arrival, sophisticated roof relationships, deep facades and balanced materials. Pursue carefully resolved craftsmanship and spatial complexity only where useful. Guest facilities, a pool pavilion or wellness rooms may serve the brief without becoming an amenity checklist. These are flexible inspirations, not requirements or price-derived promises.","capabilities":"Translate selected ideas into actual supported scene operations, with coordinated floors, enclosures, openings, entrances, roofs and terraces. Craftsmanship and spatial quality remain design intentions until supported by geometry and review. Disclose missing access, interiors and other unsupported capabilities; a price label does not prove quality.","sources":[{"kind":"curated","note":"User-supplied qualitative expectations. Location, land value, waterfront access, market conditions and construction costs can dominate price; these bands are not market evidence.","verified":false,"reference":"User brief: AI Architect — Property Value Recipes & Live Architectural Development, 2026-10-28"},{"kind":"curated","note":"Verified directly against the current user instruction: these are user-authorized subjective design-ambition references, with flexible examples and creative freedom. This source verifies curation intent only; it supplies no market-price, valuation or construction-cost evidence.","verified":true,"reference":"User instruction, Codex conversation 2026-10-28; recorded in docs/villa-playground/redesign-live/authorized-recipe-brief.md"}],"construction":{"supports":"Coordinate supporting enclosure and roof/floor datums atomically; entrances and terraces need actual connections and access.","materials":"Select available materials and facade depth for local character and maintainability; conceptual finishes do not prove craftsmanship.","operations":["add","replace","move","resize","finish"],"unsupported":"No valuation, construction-cost estimate, automatic programme, engineering, services, code or luxury certification.","requiredKinds":["plate","wall","roof"]}}
{"id":"estate-composition","version":1,"category":"composition","when":"Large private residences with substantial entertaining and service needs.","title":"Estate programme and hierarchy","combinations":"Consider guest accommodation and wellness only after a complete main residence.","placement":"Sequence arrival, entrance, living, shaded terrace and view; separate service access and private suites.","principles":"Give secondary volumes a programme and subordinate them to the residence.","capabilities":"Compose plates, walls, openings and roofs freely; no prescribed wing arrangement.","sources":[{"reference":"src/lib/villa/scene/designGuide.ts","kind":"repository","verified":true,"note":"Curated contextual application of the existing design guide; capability claims checked against scene/terra.ts and component-registry.ts."}],"construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","wall","roof"],"materials":"Choose among ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage to suit the brief; no custom textures or specialist material certification.","supports":"Connect floors, enclosure, actual openings and overhead shelter as applicable; align supports and datums. Elevated decks need guards and actual access.","unsupported":"Compose plates, walls, openings and roofs freely; no prescribed wing arrangement. No automatic circulation, engineering, service equipment or code compliance verification."}}
{"id":"waterfront-estate","version":1,"category":"climate-site","when":"Sites with a stated water edge or coastal view.","title":"Waterfront privacy and site sequence","combinations":"Consider view terraces and pools; docks only with suitable water access, brief and permissions.","placement":"Protect the public shore edge and setbacks; place living towards views, private suites away from public routes, vehicle arrival landward when feasible.","principles":"Do not invent a surveyed shore, flood elevation or legal setback; keep site assumptions explicit.","capabilities":"Flat site composition and water surfaces are available; no coastal terrain, flood simulation or marine engineering.","sources":[{"reference":"src/lib/villa/scene/designGuide.ts","kind":"repository","verified":true,"note":"Curated contextual application of the existing design guide; capability claims checked against scene/terra.ts and component-registry.ts."}],"construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","wall","roof"],"materials":"Choose among ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage to suit the brief; no custom textures or specialist material certification.","supports":"Connect floors, enclosure, actual openings and overhead shelter as applicable; align supports and datums. Elevated decks need guards and actual access.","unsupported":"Flat site composition and water surfaces are available; no coastal terrain, flood simulation or marine engineering. No automatic circulation, engineering, service equipment or code compliance verification."}}
{"id":"tropical-envelope","version":1,"category":"envelope","when":"Hot humid coastal or island contexts.","title":"Caribbean climate and envelope","combinations":"Pair shaded glazing with sheltered outdoor living and selective screening.","placement":"Place openings for potential cross ventilation and shelter entrances from driving rain; orientation and wind are assumptions until supplied.","principles":"Prioritize shade, weather protection and maintainable coastal materials; request local hurricane and corrosion engineering.","capabilities":"Screens, overhangs and openings can be constructed; no wind, corrosion, thermal or hurricane certification.","sources":[{"reference":"src/lib/villa/scene/designGuide.ts","kind":"repository","verified":true,"note":"Curated contextual application of the existing design guide; capability claims checked against scene/terra.ts and component-registry.ts."}],"construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["wall"],"materials":"Choose among ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage to suit the brief; no custom textures or specialist material certification.","supports":"Connect floors, enclosure, actual openings and overhead shelter as applicable; align supports and datums. Elevated decks need guards and actual access.","unsupported":"Screens, overhangs and openings can be constructed; no wind, corrosion, thermal or hurricane certification. No automatic circulation, engineering, service equipment or code compliance verification."}}
{"id":"living-view","version":1,"category":"programme","when":"Principal shared rooms with a stated outlook.","title":"Living room and view hierarchy","combinations":"Balance wide glazing with solid furniture walls.","placement":"Connect living to dining and a covered terrace with framed view openings.","principles":"Avoid exposed glass on every side.","capabilities":"plate, segmented wall openings, glazing and roof overhang; no glare simulation.","sources":[{"reference":"src/lib/villa/scene/terra.ts","kind":"repository","verified":true,"note":"Operation availability checked against the direct-scene contract. Design guidance is conceptual curation, not a verified regulation or external research."}],"construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","wall","roof"],"materials":"Choose among ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage to suit the brief; no custom textures or specialist material certification.","supports":"Connect floors, enclosure, actual openings and overhead shelter as applicable; align supports and datums. Elevated decks need guards and actual access.","unsupported":"plate, segmented wall openings, glazing and roof overhang; no glare simulation. No automatic circulation, engineering, service equipment or code compliance verification."}}
{"id":"legacy-recipe-15dd352f-73be-4803-a630-d590ba125c97","version":1,"category":"arrival","when":"Existing entry-sequence recipe; original compatible scales: family, luxury.","title":"Modern Tropical Driveway Threshold 01","combinations":"[{\"kind\":\"requires\",\"note\":\"form a clear vehicle approach from the site entry\",\"target\":\"driveway\"},{\"kind\":\"requires\",\"note\":\"terminate on the protected pedestrian arrival route\",\"target\":\"entry\"},{\"kind\":\"prefers\",\"note\":\"provide a direct branch before the main entry threshold\",\"target\":\"garage\"},{\"kind\":\"prefers\",\"note\":\"use planting to screen parking and frame the approach\",\"target\":\"arrival-garden\"},{\"kind\":\"prefers\",\"note\":\"coordinate low-glare guidance lighting along edges\",\"target\":\"lighting\"},{\"kind\":\"conflicts\",\"note\":\"keep vehicle circulation separate from pool access\",\"target\":\"pool\"}]","placement":"Align the approach toward a framed view of the entrance rather than the garage door. Use a widened turning bay that doubles as a discreet guest drop-off. Set the gate back from the property line to create a vehicle holding apron. Use permeable pale paving with a salt-resistant finish suitable for beach conditions. Layer palms and coastal planting at the edges without narrowing vehicle clearance. Keep bollards low, warm, and shielded from ocean-facing views. Separate the pedestrian route with a raised planted island or textured paving band.","principles":"Adapt approved guidance to the brief. Parameter options: [{\"key\":\"drivewayWidth\",\"max\":7.2,\"min\":4.8,\"unit\":\"m\",\"value\":5.8},{\"key\":\"arrivalLength\",\"max\":42,\"min\":14,\"unit\":\"m\",\"value\":24},{\"key\":\"turningDiameter\",\"max\":16,\"min\":9,\"unit\":\"m\",\"value\":12},{\"key\":\"pavingJointWidth\",\"max\":0.025,\"min\":0.006,\"unit\":\"m\",\"value\":0.012},{\"key\":\"permeablePaving\",\"unit\":\"boolean\",\"value\":true},{\"key\":\"pavingFinish\",\"unit\":\"string\",\"value\":\"sand-toned-stone\",\"options\":[\"sand-toned-stone\",\"exposed-aggregate\",\"large-format-concrete\",\"coral-limestone\"]},{\"key\":\"gateType\",\"unit\":\"string\",\"value\":\"recessed-sliding\",\"options\":[\"none\",\"recessed-sliding\",\"pivot-gate\",\"timber-screen-gate\"]},{\"key\":\"bollardSpacing\",\"max\":6,\"min\":3,\"unit\":\"m\",\"value\":4.5},{\"key\":\"arrivalLighting\",\"max\":35,\"min\":8,\"unit\":\"lux\",\"value\":18}].","capabilities":"Required capabilities: . Check against the scene construction contract; approval does not implement capabilities.","sources":[{"reference":"library recipe 15dd352f-73be-4803-a630-d590ba125c97","note":"Existing recipe approval; no new external verification.","kind":"repository","verified":false}],"construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","wall","roof"],"materials":"Choose among ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage to suit the brief; no custom textures or specialist material certification.","supports":"Connect floors, enclosure, actual openings and overhead shelter as applicable; align supports and datums. Elevated decks need guards and actual access.","unsupported":"Required capabilities: . Check against the scene construction contract; approval does not implement capabilities. No automatic circulation, engineering, service equipment or code compliance verification."}}
{"id":"legacy-recipe-3b2b038a-d096-4f7d-a405-001fb1493795","version":1,"category":"roof-outdoor","when":"Existing roof recipe; original compatible scales: family, luxury.","title":"Modern Tropical Ventilated Mono-Pitch Roof 01","combinations":"[{\"kind\":\"requires\",\"note\":\"cover primary living pavilion\",\"target\":\"main-house\"},{\"kind\":\"prefers\",\"note\":\"extend low eave over outdoor seating\",\"target\":\"covered-terrace\"},{\"kind\":\"prefers\",\"note\":\"direct visible downpipes and overflow away from entries\",\"target\":\"rain-garden\"},{\"kind\":\"prefers\",\"note\":\"orient high clerestory edge toward pool and ocean views\",\"target\":\"pool\"},{\"kind\":\"conflicts\",\"note\":\"avoid low eaves over vehicle turning paths\",\"target\":\"driveway\"}]","placement":"Slope the roof away from prevailing ocean winds where site geometry allows. Lift the high edge toward the principal view without exposing occupied rooms to direct afternoon sun. Use a continuous ventilated ridge and insect-screened clerestory gap. Extend deep eaves over glazed walls and covered outdoor living zones. Collect roof runoff in concealed gutters and route overflow to planted drainage. Keep the roof silhouette as one disciplined plane with restrained structural expression.","principles":"Adapt approved guidance to the brief. Parameter options: [{\"key\":\"roofPitch\",\"max\":20,\"min\":5,\"unit\":\"deg\",\"value\":12},{\"key\":\"eaveDepth\",\"max\":3.5,\"min\":1.2,\"unit\":\"m\",\"value\":2.4},{\"key\":\"ridgeVentHeight\",\"max\":0.9,\"min\":0.2,\"unit\":\"m\",\"value\":0.45},{\"key\":\"roofProjectionLength\",\"max\":28,\"min\":7,\"unit\":\"m\",\"value\":14},{\"key\":\"clerestoryBandHeight\",\"max\":1.5,\"min\":0.35,\"unit\":\"m\",\"value\":0.8},{\"key\":\"rainwaterTankCapacity\",\"max\":30000,\"min\":3000,\"unit\":\"L\",\"value\":12000},{\"key\":\"roofFinish\",\"value\":\"standing-seam-metal\",\"options\":[\"standing-seam-metal\",\"light-toned-tile\",\"composite-shingle\"]},{\"key\":\"ceilingFinish\",\"value\":\"timber-soffit\",\"options\":[\"timber-soffit\",\"painted-fiber-cement\",\"bamboo-lining\"]}].","capabilities":"Required capabilities: . Check against the scene construction contract; approval does not implement capabilities.","sources":[{"reference":"library recipe 3b2b038a-d096-4f7d-a405-001fb1493795","note":"Existing recipe approval; no new external verification.","kind":"repository","verified":false}],"construction":{"operations":["add","attach","place-on","finish"],"requiredKinds":["plate","wall","roof"],"materials":"Choose among ivory, limestone, timber, bronze and sage to suit the brief; no custom textures or specialist material certification.","supports":"Connect floors, enclosure, actual openings and overhead shelter as applicable; align supports and datums. Elevated decks need guards and actual access.","unsupported":"Required capabilities: . Check against the scene construction contract; approval does not implement capabilities. No automatic circulation, engineering, service equipment or code compliance verification."}}
